---
description: Require exact version pinning in manifest files to reduce supply-chain risk
alwaysApply: true
---

# Exact Version Pinning

Pin every dependency to an exact version in every manifest. Floating ranges
let a compromised upstream release (a hijacked npm package) land in installs
silently. Exact pins force every version change to be an explicit,
reviewable edit.

(Carried over from tali-central's rule of the same name.)

## Always Pin

- Never introduce `^`, `~`, `>=`, `>`, `<`, `*`, `latest`, `next`, git/tag
  refs, or any unbounded range when adding or modifying a dependency.
- When bumping a dependency, change the pinned version explicitly and update
  the lockfile in the same commit so the version change is reviewed.
- Keep `package-lock.json` committed and current. The lockfile alone is not
  sufficient because it is regenerated whenever the manifest changes.

## Applies To

- `package.json`: `dependencies`, `devDependencies`, `optionalDependencies`,
  `overrides`.

## Do Not Change

- `engines.node` and other runtime/compatibility constraints — these are
  not installed at resolve time.

## Examples

```json
// Good
"framer-motion": "13.1.1"

// Bad
"framer-motion": "^13.1.1"
```
